{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch49sJ8J4txREmzdBtAJN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added `scripts/export_invoices.py` and committed it along with `out/invoices.csv` as `accdc8c`. The export wrote 8 of the 12 invoices. I left January alone; `inbox/2026-01.csv` is still uncommitted.\n\n**One difference from the customers export:** the customers script leaves out segment \"C\". The commit that added that filter (`ba9272d`) says segment C customers declined partner sharing, and the contract covers every record held on them, invoices included. So the invoices export also leaves out their invoices. It does this by looking up each invoice's customer in `tables/customers.csv`, not by using the `seg` column in `invoices.csv`.\n\nThat's because the `seg` column in `invoices.csv` doesn't match the customer's segment on most rows. If I had filtered on it the way the customers script does, invoices 9002, 9005, 9008 and 9011 would have gone to the partner. Those belong to C customers 103 and 105. It would also have held back 9001, 9004 and 9009, which belong to customers who allowed sharing. You may want to find out why that column is wrong, since anything else that reads it will make the same mistakes.\n\n**Blocked:** the automatic permission check refused one command, a script that compared the two segment columns. I did the comparison by reading both files directly instead."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":455,"cache_read_input_tokens":21301,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":455},"output_tokens":427,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-94>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T05:22:30.826Z","request_id":"req_011Ch49sHutQm9CXKpBMmmM8"}
